> histories using what people usually call a "behavioral response". You
> might have:
>
>  logit(p[i,t]) = a0 + a1*y[i,t-1]
>
> so that if y[i,t-1] = 1 then there is some increase or decrease in
> detection probability. This is called an "ephemeral" behavioral response
> -- termed that by one of Anne Chao's grad students in a Biometrics article
> around 2005 or 2006.
>
>  The standard behavioral response is something like:
>
>  logit(p[i,t]) = a0 + a1*(if individual was ever captured previously).
>
> Other models seem plausible as well.
>
> regards
> andy
